==Old English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gem-pro|ang}} {{term/t|gem-pro|*werpaną}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|ang}} {{term/t|ine-pro|*werb-}}.  Cognate with Old Frisian {{term/t|ofs|werpa}}, Old Saxon {{term/t|osx|werpan}}, Old Dutch {{term/t|odt|werpan}} (Dutch {{term/t|nl|werpen}}), Old High German {{term/t|goh|werfan}} (German {{term/t|de|werfen}}), Old Norse {{term/t|non|verpa}} (Danish {{term/t|da|verpe}}), Gothic {{term/t|got|𐍅𐌰𐌹𐍂𐍀𐌰𐌽}}.  The Indo-European root also led to Latin {{term/t|la|verbera}}, Russian {{term/t|ru|верба}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈweorpan/|lang=ang}}

